<!-- scaling, and labels) for the ZF 8HP calibration, produced by the author from static analysis. -->
<!-- It contains NO vendor firmware, binary, or calibration data: it only describes where items sit -->
<!-- in a calibration image the user must supply separately. Author's own work product. -->
<XDFFORMAT version="1.70">
  <XDFHEADER>
    <flags>0x1</flags>
    <deftitle>ZF 8HP45 E84 (GKE233, cal 8609556) - ported RE draft</deftitle>
    <description>E84 X1 (GKE233, TYPTEILENR b5yc1313, SW Z5YD7900_8HPXY_K790D, cal 8609556) XDF, ported from the E70 8646496 RE. Cal block 0x180200-0x1FFFFF of a 2 MB image; the provided E84 read is calibration-only (program region erased/0xFF). Shift lines are NATIVE E84 structure: 21 characteristics (memory order 00..20), 1&gt;2..5&gt;6 blocks at 0x1DBA68 (300 B/char), 6&gt;7 at 0x1DD304, 7&gt;8 at 0x1DD7F0 (60 B/char, downshift = +30), pedal axes {u16 15; u16[15]} at 0x1D8FA8 (32 B stride). 8200 = shift disabled (E70 used 8000). Characteristic-to-drive-mode mapping is in the missing program ROM: identify by logging. Other items ported by byte/structure match from the E70 XDF; each says so in its description. Items that could not be safely ported (mainly packed shift_press/shiftexec/shift_time internals) are omitted; a full flash read incl. the program region would allow porting the rest. Checksums are NOT handled; sign before flashing.</description>
    <author>e_work/tools/x3_build_xdf.py</author>
