  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x11B1" flags="0x0">
    <title>Radumfang - dynamic wheel circumference (mm)</title>
    <description>Dynamic wheel circumference in mm - the tyre's ROLLING circumference, not the geometric one.
Formula: pi x (rim_inch x 25.4 + 2 x width_mm x profile_pct/100) x 0.97
Worked example: 225/45R17 = 1933 mm.
If the tyre maker publishes a rolling circumference (Abrollumfang), use that value directly.
IMPORTANT: after flashing, reset the learned rear axle value (Tool32 job steuern_lernfkt_ruecksetzen, argument 0) and drive above ~24 km/h so it re-learns. Then read status_lernfkt: the learned value must equal your real diff ratio; if it is one step off (e.g. 3.91 instead of 3.73), multiply your entry by (real ratio / learned value) and repeat.
Note: the TCU only accepts the closest value from its fixed ratio list (2.00 2.35 2.47 2.56 2.65 2.81 2.93 3.08 3.15 3.23 3.38 3.46 3.64 3.73 3.91 4.10 4.27), so the entry only needs to be within about -1 %/+2.5 % of the reference.
Do not use this to correct the speedometer - that is the DSC's coding. || E84 8609556: ported from E70 by content match (manual-signature), delta -0x4b0c.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x191404" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
